  "note": "The DELE ladder begins at A1; Instituto Cervantes publishes no diploma below it, and the para escolares variants are age-adapted forms of A1 and A2/B1 rather than sub-levels. This rung is therefore project-defined per HL18 §2. The two Cervantes sources are cited to fix what this precursor runs UP TO, not to imply an official pre-A1 format exists.",
  "administration": {
    "writtenMinutes": 25,
    "speakingMinutes": 5,
    "speakingGroupMaximum": 1,
    "speakingPreparationMinutes": 2,
    "deliveryModes": [
      "paper",
      "recorded-audio",
      "live-interlocutor"
    ]
  },
  "passRule": {
    "maximumPoints": 100,
    "passPoints": 60,
    "requiresEverySectionAttempted": true,
    "independentSkillThresholds": {
      "reading": 0.6,
      "listening": 0.6,
      "writing": 0.6,
      "speaking": 0.6
    },
    "note": "Each skill is worth 25 points and must independently reach 60%; the overall 60-point floor cannot compensate for a failed skill. This is deliberately STRICTER than DELE's own grouped rule (reading+writing and listening+speaking, 30/50 per group, 60/100 overall), because a grouped rule lets a strong reader carry a weak writer and this rung exists to prove all four moved together. It is a project-defined precursor below the official DELE A1 ladder."
  },
